│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ avoid_redundant_path_reconstruction                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The incumbent update reconstructs a complete beam-history path even when the score is     │
│                          │ tied. This is extremely expensive: for incomplete trees, the actual score depends only on │
│                          │ S, so many candidates tie, while reconstructing each candidate is O(depth). Moreover, a   │
│                          │ tied incomplete score receives no benefit from a shorter move sequence; only a strictly   │
│                          │ better S can improve the official score. For a complete tree, the score already strictly  │
│                          │ improves when K decreases.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Therefore, retain the incumbent only on a strictly better actual score. This avoids a     │
│                          │ large amount of repeated history traversal and string allocation, allowing the beam       │
│                          │ search to evaluate substantially more states within the time limit.                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
