│ patch_description        │ The beam search reconstructs complete move strings for every candidate tied with the      │
│                          │ current best score. Ties are extremely common because incomplete-tree scores depend only  │
│                          │ on tree size. Since path length is exactly `next_K_total`, the existing “prefer shorter   │
│                          │ path” condition can be checked without reconstruction. This substantially reduces         │
│                          │ allocation and reverse-traversal overhead, allowing more beam iterations.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the current fixed 400 ms safety slack stops around 2.55 seconds despite a 3 │
│                          │ second limit. Reducing it moderately to 250 ms gives the search more useful iterations    │
│                          │ while retaining a conservative margin for system-test timing variation.                   │
