│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - It starts searching immediately from the given position, preserving useful structure    │
│                          │ instead of spending moves relocating the empty cell.                                      │
│                          │ - Every board is evaluated as a graph using DSU, measuring the largest acyclic component, │
│                          │ compatible edges, cyclic vertices, and component fragmentation.                           │
│                          │ - The beam objective strongly prioritizes the actual target metric (largest tree), while  │
│                          │ compatible edges provide a smoother gradient before large tree merges become available.   │
│                          │ - The next beam is selected through a mixture of strong global elites and “one best state │
│                          │ per empty-square position”, preventing all states from collapsing into identical blank    │
│                          │ trajectories.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Zobrist hashing is used for both state deduplication and score memoization.             │
│                          │ - Paths are stored as compact persistent history nodes, allowing many explored states     │
│                          │ without copying strings.                                                                  │
