│ patch_name               │ cycle_aware_edge_guidance                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Augment the evaluation with the total number of matched tile edges and the size of the    │
│                          │ largest connected component. The existing heuristic strongly rewards fewer components,    │
│                          │ but this can accidentally prefer closing cycles: a cyclic component reduces the component │
│                          │ count without contributing to the official largest-tree objective.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new score uses matched edges as a mild positive signal for assembling correct local   │
│                          │ adjacencies, while explicitly penalizing the cyclomatic excess `matched_edges - (V -      │
│                          │ components)`. This excess is zero for a forest and positive exactly when cycles exist.    │
│                          │ The largest connected-component term also supplies a useful tie-breaker among states with │
│                          │ equal largest acyclic tree and component count, favoring states that are closer to        │
│                          │ globally connected without overpowering the primary objective.                            │
